export anchor PassportNightStyle:
    number: 417
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Passport night
    idea: The trip kept in a dark passport, a data page with the holder, dates and a machine readable line, then a visa page where every itinerary leg is an inked stamp of its own shape and unbooked legs are dashed blanks waiting for ink.
    base: dark
    palette:
        desk: #0b0f14, the page and the style sheet
        cover: #13241f, the passport cover band
        leaf: #16232a, passport pages, cards and rows with faint guilloche rings
        line: #2f4a52, field rules, the photo box and page edges
        ink: #eef2ec, text
        muted: #a9b9b4, field labels, the machine line and blank stamp outlines
        gold: #f0cf6a, the emblem, section labels, the flight stamp, the route and the primary button
        stampRed: #ff9484, the Tokyo stamp
        stampTeal: #6fe0d0, the Kyoto stamp
        stampViolet: #c9b0ff, the flight home stamp
        booked: #8be3a6, Booked and Done words
        unbooked: #f6c27a, Not booked and To do words
    type:
        Georgia for page titles at 34px and figures at 40px. Helvetica Neue,
        Arial for labels at 12px caps tracked 0.2em in gold and body at
        15px. Arial Black caps for stamp text at 12 to 15px. ui-monospace
        caps for data fields at 15px and the machine line at 14px tracked
        0.12em.
    layout:
        A dark green cover band on top with a gold ringed star, BRIGHTWORK
        TRIPS in gold spaced caps and Travel document Trip 01 on the right.
        Then two passport spreads, each two pages side by side with a
        shadowed spine. Page 2 is the data page. Trip over Japan in April, a
        photo box with MO and plus 1, and fields Holder, Companions, Valid
        and Route in monospace caps. Funds shows 3,200 of 5,000 euros saved
        with a thin gold bar, then a machine readable line in a dark box.
        Page 3, Visas and entries, holds the itinerary as six stamps in a
        three column grid, each slightly rotated. The flight out is a gold
        double oval, Tokyo a red double circle, Kyoto a teal rounded square,
        the flight home a violet oval. Each stamp holds an icon, date,
        place, detail and a status word under a rule. The train and Osaka
        are dashed grey blanks with Not booked. A legend under the stamps
        explains inked and blank. The second spread holds Page 4 Endorsement
        Route, a sketch with contour lines, a coast and a dashed gold route
        between three ringed points, and Page 5 Conditions of travel with
        the checklist, a weather note with a gold left bar, and the two
        buttons. Below 900px each spread stacks its pages and at phone width
        stamps go two across.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 28 to 32px page padding, 20px between stamp rows and 32px between spreads.
    density: Medium. Two spreads of two pages and six stamps in a three column grid.
    corners: Square pages with a soft spine. Circle, oval and 10px square stamps, 2px fields and buttons.
    borders: Double borders on inked stamps, 2px dashed borders on blanks and dotted rules in the checklist.
    shadows: A spine shadow inside each page where the spread folds and a deep drop under each spread.
    icons:
        Small line icons inside stamps. Booked carries a check under a rule,
        Not booked a dashed circle in a dashed blank, and flights a plane.
        Done is a ticked box and To do a dashed empty box.
    focus: A 2px dashed gold outline offset 4px.
    tone: Official but kind, such as Visas and entries, Conditions of travel and Endorsement.
